course: dictionary
lesson: 13960
title: The word likelihood
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Likelihood means how likely something is to happen. It is a noun, so it names a thing: the chance that something will happen. «The likelihood of rain today is high» means rain is very probable.
explain: In maths, likelihood is measured on a scale from impossible to certain. The words on the scale are impossible, unlikely, even chance, likely and certain. You can also write it as a number from 0 to 1, where 0 means impossible and 1 means certain.
explain: «In all likelihood, the bus will be late» means the bus will very probably be late. This phrase is common in sentences about chances and in weather forecasts.
fact: Likelihood means how likely something is to happen.
fact: Likelihood is a noun, and it is usually not counted, so you say «the likelihood», not «the likelihoods».
fact: On a maths scale, likelihood runs from impossible (0) to certain (1).
fact: «In all likelihood» means very probably.
fact: Weather forecasts often give the likelihood of rain, such as «There is a 70% likelihood of rain.»
exercise: «The likelihood of snow tonight is high.» What does likelihood mean here? | Lots of snow will fall at once | *The chance that snow will fall | The colour of the snow | The time the snow stops
exercise: On the maths scale, which word shows a likelihood of 0? | *Impossible | Certain | Likely | Even chance
exercise: «In all likelihood, the bus will be late.» What does «in all likelihood» mean? | For sure, with no doubt at all | Long ago | *Very probably | Certainly not
test: «There is a small likelihood that the match will be cancelled.» What is a small likelihood? | Happening every day | Certain to happen | *Not very likely to happen | Happening right now
test: On the 0 to 1 scale, which number shows that something is certain? | *1 | 0 | 0.5 | 10
exam: Which phrase means the same as «increase the likelihood»? | Make it less likely | *Make it more likely | Make it a different word | Make it impossible
